      <h2>Before Zennly</h2>
      <p>Nuad Thai Spa Kathmandu grew from a single location to four branches the way most service businesses do &ndash; one good year at a time, with the booking system never catching up. Appointments were confirmed over the phone, tracked on a branch-by-branch basis, and reconciled against the till at the end of the day. It worked when there was one branch to watch. It stopped working at three.</p>
      <p>The owner&rsquo;s mornings were spent calling each branch manager individually to find out who was booked, who had shown up, and what had been collected the day before. Discounts were verbal, so a therapist could offer 15% off without anyone above them knowing until the numbers didn&rsquo;t add up. Staff moved between branches informally, which meant a manager could find out a therapist wasn&rsquo;t coming in only when the client was already in the waiting room.</p>

      <h2>What changed</h2>
      <p>Zennly replaced the phone-and-spreadsheet system with a single operational layer across all four branches. Every booking now moves through the same lifecycle &ndash; Pending, Confirmed, In-Progress, Completed &ndash; visible in real time to whoever needs to see it, at whatever level they&rsquo;re allowed to see it at.</p>
      <h3>Booking &amp; scheduling</h3>
      <p>Front-desk staff create bookings directly against a specific therapist and room. Conflicts are prevented at the database level, not caught after the fact by a manager comparing notebooks.</p>
      <h3>Discount control</h3>
      <p>A therapist can still offer a discount &ndash; but it&rsquo;s a request, not a decision. It only applies once a manager approves it, and every request carries the exact percentage and amount. The spa&rsquo;s pricing strategy now survives contact with the front desk.</p>
      <h3>Staff transfers</h3>
      <p>When a therapist moves between branches, it&rsquo;s a scheduled event with an effective date &ndash; not a phone call the morning of. Managers at both branches see the change coming.</p>
      <h3>Daily reconciliation</h3>
      <p>Every payment is logged at the point of service, against the booking it belongs to. The owner&rsquo;s morning call round has been replaced by a single dashboard that&rsquo;s already correct.</p>

      <blockquote>&ldquo;I used to spend my mornings calling every branch. Now I open the platform and everything is already there.&rdquo;</blockquote>

      <h2>The result</h2>
      <p>Across the four branches, Nuad Thai Spa now runs roughly 350 bookings and 170 recorded payments a week through Zennly, with every discount request and staff transfer carrying its own audit trail. Nothing about the business got simpler &ndash; four branches, 39 therapists, and 194 services is still a lot to run. What changed is that the owner sees it as one operation instead of four separate ones held together by phone calls.</p>

